{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.domain` is a trait contract. It has these obligations: the trait's shape and bounds, a cloneable domain that is safe to share between executions, `Send` storage futures, and defaults for the three optional source methods.\n\n- **Bounds and signatures.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` implements `Domain` for a fixture type, `Relationships`. Its error type is `Send` but not `Sync`, and its node data and labels are opaque. The nested `check_bounds<G: Domain>` helper is generic over the trait. It requires these bounds of the generic parameter:\n  - The domain is `Clone + Send + Sync`.\n  - `NodeData` is `Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`.\n  - `EdgeLabel` is `Clone + Send + Sync`.\n  - `Error` is `Send`.\n  - `NodeContent` is `NodeContents + Send + Sync`.\n  - The `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures are `Send`.\n  \n  A weaker or stronger bound would fail to compile. The test calls the required methods with the trait's signatures.\n- **Method behaviour.** The same test checks the following:\n  - `node_content` returns content with `format() == \"1\"` and a fingerprint value of `\"1\"`.\n  - `load_evidence` returns `None` for a missing record, and `store_evidence` succeeds.\n  - `node_path` gives distinct paths for different nodes.\n  - `outgoing_edges` returns the expected successors per label, an empty list for unknown labels, and an error for an invalid node.\n- **Optional-method defaults.** `domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled` and the `Relationships` assertions both check that `project_sources()` returns `None` and `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`. The first also checks that `source_address` returns `None`. The statement text does not specify `source_node`'s default behaviour, so asserting `Invalid` adds a check rather than leaving a gap.\n- **Cloneable and safe to share between executions.**\n  - `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`, `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls` and `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces` use one domain across concurrent executions.\n  - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` also shares a domain, and it asserts that the records stay independent.\n  - `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` checks `assert_send_sync` on the context.\n  - `check_bounds` enforces `Clone + Send + Sync` on the domain at compile time.\n- **Domains working end to end.** `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`, `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer`, `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` and `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` use domains for content, edges and evidence storage, and they assert the outcomes.\n\nThe required behaviour is covered, and every test reviewed carries a `{test}` marker. I found no gap.",
  "references": "1219af9c261c7c256deaf030045562c41b04d884087245d89e34d2f09aa8f735",
